, BM were green (3).\n- I clicked ML \u2192 ML became green (all 4 green = complete diamond) \u2192 this triggered the shrink + reset.\nSo the mechanic might be: when all 4 edge-mids are green (matching the purple diamond in the left box), the block shrinks and the box resets.\nBut wait, in the previous run, after clicking ML, the tiles all became gray (not green). So the \"all 4 green\" state triggered the shrink and then reset the tiles to gray.\nHmm, but actually the tiles' base colors are: edge-mids = white, corners+center = gray. After the reset, they were all gray. That's weird \u2014 the edge-mids should be white, not gray.\nWait, let me reconsider. After the shrink in the previous run, the state was: TM=g, ML=g, MR=g, BM=g, C=g (all gray). But the initial state has edge-mids white, corners+center gray. So after the shrink, the edge-mids became gray (not white). That's a change from the initial state.\nHmm, that's confusing. Let me reconsider.\nActually, maybe the \"reset\" after the shrink set all tiles to gray (a different state). Or maybe the shrink changed the tile colors.\nThis is getting complicated. Let me take a cleaner approach: let me reproduce the shrink in this fresh run and carefully observe what happens to the block, bar, and tiles.\nLet me set up: make TM, MR, BM green, then click ML, and observe.\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider whether the shrink is triggered by \"all 4 edge-mids green\" or by something else. Let me test more carefully.\nLet me first make all 4 edge-mids green and see if the block shrinks (without clicking a 5th tile).\nPlan:\n1. Click TM, MR, BM, ML (all 4 edge-mids) \u2192 all green.\n2. Observe: does the block shrink? Do the tiles reset?\nLet me do this step by step to see exactly when the shrink happens.\nActually, let me click them one at a time and observe after each:\n1. Click TM \u2192 observe.\n2. Click MR \u2192 observe.\n3. Click BM \u2192 observe.\n4. Click ML \u2192 observe.\nThis will tell me exactly which click triggers the shrink (if any).\nLet me do this.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "Tiles are simple toggles (W\u2194N green); block/bar unchanged by a single toggle. The shrink must trigger on a specific configuration. Let me set all 4 edge-mids green one at a time, observing after each click to pinpoint the trigger.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\ndef state(frame):\n    a=frame.ascii.split('\\n')\n    pts=[(r,c) for r in range(17,24) for c in range(17,44) if a[r][c] in ('b','S')]\n    cs=[p[1] for p in pts]; rs=[p[0] for p in pts]\n    blk=(min(rs),max(rs),min(cs),max(cs))\n    from collections import Counter\n    def tmaj(r0,c0): return Counter(a[r][c] for r in range(r0,r0+3) for c in range(c0,c0+3)).most_common(1)[0][0]\n    tiles={'TM':tmaj(49,29),'ML':tmaj(54,24),'MR':tmaj(54,34),'BM':tmaj(59,29),'C':tmaj(54,29)}\n    return blk,tiles\nfor name,(r,c) in [('TM',(50,30)),('MR',(55,35)),('BM',(60,30)),('ML',(55,25))]:\n    action([{'action':'MOUSE','row':r,'col':c}])\n    print(f\"after {name}:\",state(current_frame), last_action_result.get('board_changed'))\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "after TM: ((19, 22, 39, 42), {'TM': 'N', 'ML': 'W', 'MR': 'W', 'BM': 'W', 'C': 'g'}) True\nafter MR: ((19, 22, 39, 42), {'TM': 'N', 'ML': 'W', 'MR': 'N', 'BM': 'W', 'C': 'g'}) True\nafter BM: ((19, 22, 39, 42), {'TM': 'N', 'ML': 'W', 'MR': 'N', 'BM': 'N', 'C': 'g'}) True\nafter ML: ((19, 20, 39, 40), {'TM': 'g', 'ML': 'g', 'MR': 'g', 'BM': 'g', 'C': 'g'}) True", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}], "hasExactModelContext": false, "requestIndexWithinTurn": null, "messageCount": 0}, "context": {"sections": [{"label": "USER PROMPT", "content": "The code executed 2 actions in the previous sequence.\nExecuted actions: MOUSE(row=50, col=30), MOUSE(r